‹Heading1,b:Review drawer›
‹Rule:────────────────────›

‹Code: leader d › slides a
‹Text,b:review drawer› in
from the right over
half the body and
shows the focused
pane's diff: an
agent's ‹Text,i:last turn›,
or its branch
against the base.
See the ‹Link,u:design notes›
for the keys; it
replaces ‹Text,s:the old›
‹Text,s:layout pane›. Press
‹Key,b:esc› to hand the
keyboard back.

‹AlertNote:▎ ›‹AlertNote,b:󰋽 Note›
‹AlertNote:▎ ›The panes under
‹AlertNote:▎ ›the drawer keep
‹AlertNote:▎ ›their size, so no
‹AlertNote:▎ ›agent redraws when
‹AlertNote:▎ ›it opens or
‹AlertNote:▎ ›closes.

‹Heading2,b:What changed›

  ‹Bullet:• ›The ported tuios
    ‹Code: diffview › draws
    the lines, with
    highlighting
    from the theme
  ‹Bullet:• ›One watcher per
    worktree, shared
    by every agent
    in it
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›the turn gate
      skips
      unchanged
      snapshots
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›the agents
      rail re-probes
      on a branch
      switch
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›which fixes
        the stale
        ‹Code: main › on
        the cards
  ‹Bullet:• ›‹Code: leader n › picks
    a worktree for a
    new agent
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›‹Image:󰥶 The drawer ›‹Image:…›
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›‹SummaryMark,b:▸ ›‹Summary,b:Keys in the›
        ‹Summary,b:list›
        ‹FoldHint:enter opens›

‹Heading3,b:Checklist›

  ‹TaskDone,b:✓ ›‹Code: make check ›
    ‹TaskDoneText:passes›
  ‹TaskDone,b:✓ ›‹TaskDoneText:Goldens in Mocha›
    ‹TaskDoneText:and Latte›
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›The macOS CI
    step for the
    watcher fix

‹Heading2,b:How to test›

  ‹Bullet:1. ›Open three
     agents in
     master-stack:
     ‹Code: leader n ›
     three times
  ‹Bullet:2. ›Run a prompt in
     the master,
     then press
     ‹Code: leader d ›
  ‹Bullet:3. ›Step through
     the turns with
     ‹Code: , › and ‹Code: . ›

